andrew lansley there are mounting a  defense of public health england  now in august last year the 19 year old  harry dahn was killed when his motorbike  crashed into a car outside a u.s  military base  in northamptonshire anne takulis the  wife of a u.s intelligence official was  involved in the crash she fled back to  the u.s  claiming diplomatic immunity it sparked  an international row with an extradition  request lodged by the uk government  rejected by washington back in january  and tomorrow the man who turned down  that request  the u.s secretary of state mike pompeo  will be in london to meet the foreign  secretary dominic raab  harry's mother charlotte charles has a  message for the two men  and she joins us now um thank you so  much for being  on the uh this morning i know this must  be an incredibly difficult thing  to talk about um charlotte how  difficult have the 11 months been since  harry's death  oh my goodness sophie i don't even know  where we would even try to begin  uh beyond excruciating every single day  you know we have to wake up every  morning knowing that harry isn't with us  and we have to try to live with that  you dream about him at night time and  you wake up and you feel angry and  bitter that we've been left with our  with our family in complete tatters and  in ruin  and still don't have justice for him  we're tired  um so still very much determined  to get that justice the determination  still burns extremely strong  but we're tired and we need the uk  to work really hard really hard with the  us government now and  and bring a closure to this bring her  back and  get that justice and do not allow us and  force us to go into a second year of  fighting  i just want to say how much i appreciate  you talking about this i know how  difficult it must be we really do  appreciate you you know  talking about such a horrific experience  for yourself and your family  um of course nothing could make up for  losing harry but  how important would it meet be how much  would it mean to you  for anne sir coolest to return to the  united kingdom  everything absolutely everything  that promise i made to my boy the night  we lost him  needs to be filled it needs to be  fulfilled it needs to be completed it  has to be  it's the only way it's the right way  it's the right thing to do  everybody no matter what crime's been  committed  expects justice and and this is a case  that shouldn't be any different to that  you know we all agree that diplomatic  community needs to be  in place for the right circumstances  this isn't one of those circumstances  this  isn't something that they would be  setting a precedent for  by sending her back this is something  that immunity does not  cover it needs to be  done justice needs to be done i need  that justice to be done the whole of our  family needs  the right thing to be done and we need  to feel  that heaven forbid should  ever happen to another family which  we're working desperately hard to try  and make sure it doesn't  that family would need to feel like the  uk are on their side  it's so important to feel supported by  your own government  and unfortunately we we just haven't had  that  but it's never too late so just help  help us  help us help us get this promise  completed  please mr secretary just to turn to you  um the uk government has filed an  extradition request  to the united states and the prime  minister and the foreign secretary have  also raised the issue with president  trump and also with  the secretary of state pompeo a number  of times they say  what more practically can the uk  government do  sophie good morning and again just thank  you so much for having us on i can't  tell you how much  it means to the family and to have this  platform to speak  directly to those in power so thank you  again it it  it's very very simple what now needs to  happen because we've had  lots of words um we've had  tons of support from the media and the  millions of people around the world  but what we now need from mr johnson mr  rob as  secretary pompeo comes tomorrow is  action  and what we want now and i've asked this  of mr rob  several times is a very clear uh  timetabled structured plan to bring and  seculas back it is no longer  any good and i'm sure if he's coming on  he'll tell you the same that they raise  it continually  that means nothing to the family let's  not forget  that almost a year ago an american  citizen  took the life of a british citizen and  was allowed to walk away  she needs to come back actions have  consequences  this is one of the most egregious abuses  of human rights  america has ever committed um  on a british citizen a british family  where is the special relationship  there must be consequences so what are  we going to do  are we going to expel diplomats are we  going to expel  the ambassador are we going to impose  sanctions  are we going to stop extraditions the  other way because there's there is no  reciprocity  if mr rob can come forward this morning  and speak  speak to us and tell us what he is going  to do in clear  specific terms and he usually comes on  these programs with a pre-prepared  script  so sophie please don't let him wriggle  out of this a  clear specific plan if the united states  are not going to send her back what is  the united kingdom going to do  with specificity to make sure  that that this terrible wrong is righted  are you worried at all i heard you say  there what special relationship  are you worried at all that particularly  with such a volatile  president that the uk government feels  that they can't  they need to keep america on side at  such a  important time in global affairs with  you know from china to russia to iran  absolutely sophie and we are very well  aware of the  geostrategic imperatives here and the  sensitivities  but what have we come to when  we lose a child and and both governments  effectively ask this family  to walk on by as far as we're concerned  i know we've got 5g and huawei and hong  kong and  russia and china to worry about as  secretary pompeo visits  but as far as we're concerned harry  has to be number one on the agenda this  is about human rights  and america professes to be the champion  of human rights  um how can secretary pompeo come here  this week with a straight face and  preach to the world  about human rights when you've got the  most gorgeous family my dear friends  who live 300 yards up the road from me  um  suffering terribly it's hypocrisy in the  extreme so we're very well aware of  those tensions  but this is the united kingdom's  opportunity uh  mr robb's opportunity to show the nation  that he is going to fulfill his first  duty  which is to safeguard and protect the  lives of uk citizens  we've got a uk citizen sitting right  next to me he needs to stand up to the  united states now  uh everything will be fine when  antsakulis comes back the world is not  going to fall apart  no precedent will be set but what will  happen  is we can give this family the  opportunity to get the justice that they  so desperately need  and then the closure and then sophie  then we can all move on and go back to  those terribly important  uh global affairs that you that you just  mentioned okay thank you  uh both so much for being on the  programme  in particular thank you to you charlotte  as well for talking about something that  i know  is incredibly difficult thank you thank  you

